  "notes": "University Park. Built from the archived 2022-2023 bulletin's Suggested Academic Plan and Program Requirements tabs (fetched raw HTML and cross-checked semester credit subtotals against the page's own printed per-term totals, summing to the stated 131-credit total). This pre-2025 curriculum is genuinely different from ENGY-2026.json in the third and fourth years: EGEE 12 (Energy Science and Engineering Lectures, 1cr) and MATSE 201 (Introduction to Materials Science, 3cr) were required courses here, not 'Material Science elective' options (that elective category doesn't exist in this era's plan at all -- MATSE 201 is simply mandatory); EGEE 451 was required outright with no 'or ENVSE 470' alternative; FSC 431 and FSC 432 (Fuel Science) were required fixed courses, not a 'Fuel Science elective' slot; a required 2-credit EGEE 494/295/395/495 (Research Project or Internship, instructor's choice of course number per the bulletin's own 'or' phrasing) replaced one of 2026's Technical Elective slots; and EGEE 438 was a required fixed course rather than one option within an 'Energy Systems elective' slot (that elective category, like Material Science and Fuel Science, doesn't exist in this era's plan). The bulletin's own Fourth Year spring row also names an 'EGEE Elective from Approved Department List' category with no explicit course list published anywhere on the program page and no surviving department Approved Electives snapshot for this era -- left as an unenforced generic placeholder (same convention as CMPSC-2022.json's own unverifiable elective-pool slots) rather than guessing which EGEE courses qualified. Professional elective and Technical elective slots reuse ENGY-2026.json's own verified match regexes since those category names and the department's course pools they draw from (ACCTG/BA/BLAW/EBF/ENGR/ERM/GEOG/IB for Professional; AE/CE/CHE/EE/EGEE/EME/ENVSE/ESC/GEOG/MATSE/ME/METEO/MNG/MNPR/NUCE/PNG for Technical) are university-wide course-catalog categories, not major-curriculum content that changed between eras -- unlike the MATSE 201/FSC 431/FSC 432/EGEE 438/EGEE 451 changes above, which are genuine curriculum-structure differences confirmed directly against this year's own printed plan table. Semesters 1-2 and 3-4 (First and Second Year) are course-for-course identical to ENGY-2026.json -- verified directly against this year's own archived table -- so carried forward unchanged, including the same CHEM 110 -> MATH 22 -> MATH 21 / MATH 4 -> MATH 3 real-prereq-chain fix from the 2026 file's own notes (this app's course-catalog/prereq data is scraped once, not per catalog-year, so the same fix applies here).",
